  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Δ</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If the angle bisector of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∠</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> meets the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math>, then the length of the projection of the vector <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></math> on the vector <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></math> is:"
  },
